# Calculator, Edit > Paste in the scientific view: ":5F0&3C|1^FF=~<4=" (Hex by its paste code, And,
# Or, Xor, Not, Lsh), then the word sizes Word, Byte and Dword
# Port side: the text goes onto the clipboard with "clip"; the reference frames come from
# calc-paste3.scn (Program Manager shell, Notepad copies the text; its frames before
# Calculator pastes are not compared, only those of Calculator's window); recorded with
# dosbox-x_MinGWx64_SDL2.exe (its FPU computes with the host x87, as a real 387 would).
# regress: ARCH311_APP=apps/build/calc sh tools/run-cp-test.sh "$TEST" "$OUT"
# compare: calc-paste3/01.png 01.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste3/02.png 02.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste3/03.png 03.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste3/04.png 04.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste3/05.png 05.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: calc-paste3/06.png 06.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# ini: WIN.INI SciCalc layout=0
sleep 400
sleep 400
shot shots/01.png
key alt
key v
key s
sleep 400
shot shots/02.png
clip :5F0&3C|1^FF=~<4=
key alt
key e
key p
sleep 400
shot shots/03.png
key f3
sleep 400
shot shots/04.png
key f4
sleep 400
shot shots/05.png
key f2
sleep 400
shot shots/06.png
